}"}, {"type": "output_text", "tool_name": null, "arguments": null, "output": "Explanation: The clues point to Filipino teen actor AJ Perez (Antonello Joseph Sarte Perez), who died at age 18 on April 17, 2011, when the van he was riding in collided with a bus in Moncada, Tarlac—a vehicular accident within the 2008–2016 window [98388]. He was the only fatality; everyone else in the vehicle survived, including his father Gerardo Perez and the driver Christopher Bautista [98388]. After his death, his parents Gerry and Marivic Perez decided to donate his corneas (the tissue of his eyes, a paired set of organs) to the EyeBank Foundation of the Philippines [5784]. His two corneas went to two recipients: Lawrence Villanueva, then 28, and an unnamed 8-year-old boy [92091]. That child was John Daniel delos Santos, who had the transplant in April 2011 [5784]. Prior to 2023—on October 27, 2020—the then-17-year-old John Daniel appeared as a guest on the "Eat Bulaga" segment "Bawal Judgemental," revealed he was the recipient of AJ Perez's cornea, and expressed his lifelong gratitude to AJ and his parents [5784].

